What coffee equipment do you have at home? → Drip or filter machine
Do you want it hot or iced? → Hot
@say
My pick is a strong black filter coffee made in your drip machine.

Recipe (one large mug, about 350 ml):
- Coffee: 27 g, which is about 4½ tablespoons. Use a dark or medium-dark roast. A normal mug uses about 21 g, so this makes it stronger.
- Water: 350 ml of cold, filtered water.
- Grind: Medium-fine, slightly finer than standard filter grind. The finer grind gives more body.
- Brew: Run a normal cycle. Drink it right away, because the hot plate turns the coffee bitter after about 20 minutes.

For an even bolder cup: Use 30 g of coffee. Do not cut the water instead, because a very small batch extracts badly in most drip machines.

Do you buy pre-ground coffee or whole beans? With pre-ground coffee, you can't change the grind, so add the extra coffee instead.
